{"code":"43-5061.00","title":"Production, Planning, and Expediting Clerks","description":"Coordinate and expedite the flow of work and materials within or between departments of an establishment according to production schedule. Duties include reviewing and distributing production, work, and shipment schedules; conferring with department supervisors to determine progress of work and completion dates; and compiling reports on progress of work, inventory levels, costs, and production problems.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":3.12,"share":0.171},"I":{"score":1.2,"share":0.0161},"A":{"score":1.14,"share":0.0113},"S":{"score":2.11,"share":0.0895},"E":{"score":4.91,"share":0.3153},"C":{"score":5.92,"share":0.3968}},"highPoints":["C","E"],"tasks":[{"id":11370,"text":"Distribute production schedules or work orders to departments.","core":true,"importance":4.35,"relevance":81.73,"frequency":4.95},{"id":11365,"text":"Revise production schedules when required due to design changes, labor or material shortages, backlogs, or other interruptions, collaborating with management, marketing, sales, production, or engineering.","core":true,"importance":4.29,"relevance":74.64,"frequency":4.6},{"id":11363,"text":"Review documents, such as production schedules, work orders, or staffing tables, to determine personnel or materials requirements or material priorities.","core":true,"importance":4.16,"relevance":73.7,"frequency":4.8},{"id":11372,"text":"Arrange for delivery, assembly, or distribution of supplies or parts to expedite flow of materials and meet production schedules.","core":true,"importance":3.99,"relevance":82.19,"frequency":4.61},{"id":11366,"text":"Confer with establishment personnel, vendors, or customers to coordinate production or shipping activities and to resolve complaints or eliminate delays.","core":true,"importance":3.98,"relevance":68.1,"frequency":4.74},{"id":11368,"text":"Requisition and maintain inventories of materials or supplies necessary to meet production demands.","core":true,"importance":3.94,"relevance":76.99,"frequency":4.29},{"id":11364,"text":"Confer with department supervisors or other personnel to assess progress and discuss needed changes.","core":true,"importance":3.86,"relevance":95.01,"frequency":4.6},{"id":11362,"text":"Examine documents, materials, or products and monitor work processes to assess completeness, accuracy, and conformance to standards and specifications.","core":false,"importance":3.85,"relevance":60.26,"frequency":4.37},{"id":11375,"text":"Plan production commitments or timetables for business units, specific programs, or jobs, using sales forecasts.","core":true,"importance":3.78,"relevance":68.03,"frequency":4.3},{"id":11371,"text":"Compile information, such as production rates and progress, materials inventories, materials used, or customer information, so that status reports can be completed.","core":true,"importance":3.77,"relevance":77.6,"frequency":4.2},{"id":11377,"text":"Compile and prepare documentation related to production sequences, transportation, personnel schedules, or purchase, maintenance, or repair orders.","core":false,"importance":3.68,"relevance":57.78,"frequency":4.3},{"id":11369,"text":"Calculate figures, such as required amounts of labor or materials, manufacturing costs, or wages, using pricing schedules, adding machines, calculators, or computers.","core":false,"importance":3.67,"relevance":47.83,"frequency":4.24},{"id":11373,"text":"Contact suppliers to verify shipment details.","core":false,"importance":3.63,"relevance":49.83,"frequency":3.74},{"id":11367,"text":"Record production data, including volume produced, consumption of raw materials, or quality control measures.","core":false,"importance":3.45,"relevance":65.89,"frequency":4.16},{"id":11376,"text":"Establish and prepare product construction directions and locations and information on required tools, materials, equipment, numbers of workers needed, and cost projections.","core":false,"importance":3.3